1
00:05:36,666 --> 00:05:42,666
Pray Away is a documentary film directed by Kristine Stolakis.

2
00:11:13,333 --> 00:11:19,333
In the 1970s, five men struggling with being gay in their Evangelical church started a bible study to help each other leave the "homosexual lifestyle." They quickly received over
25,000 letters from people asking for help and formalized as Exodus International, the largest and most controversial conversion therapy organization in the world.

3
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:56,000
But leaders struggled with a secret: their own
“same-sex attractions” never went away.

4
00:22:26,666 --> 00:22:32,666
After years as Christian superstars in the religious right, many of these men and women
have come out as LGBTQ, disavowing the very movement they helped start.

5
00:28:03,333 --> 00:28:09,333
Focusing on the dramatic journeys of former conversion therapy leaders, current members, and a survivor, PRAY AWAY
chronicles the “ex gay" movement’s rise to power, persistent influence, and the profound harm it causes.

6
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Self, played by Julie Rodgers.

7
00:39:16,666 --> 00:39:22,666
Self, played by Randy Thomas.

8
00:44:53,333 --> 00:44:59,333
Self, played by Yvette Cantu Schneider.

9
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Self, played by John Paulk.

10
00:56:06,666 --> 00:56:12,666
Self, played by Jeffrey McCall.

11
01:01:43,333 --> 01:01:49,333
Self, played by Alan Chambers.

12
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Pray Away is a 2021 American documentary film
produced and directed by Kristine Stolakis.

13
01:12:56,666 --> 01:13:02,666
It follows survivors of conversion therapy, and former leaders.

14
01:18:33,333 --> 01:18:39,333
Jason Blum and Ryan Murphy serve as executive producers.

15
01:24:10,000 --> 01:24:16,000
It had its world premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival on June 16, 2021.

16
01:29:46,666 --> 01:29:52,666
It was released on August 3, 2021, by Netflix.

17
01:35:23,333 --> 01:35:29,333
The film explores themes of homophobia, guilt, lgbt,
woman director, conversion therapy.
